  "query_preview": "..\n\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Summer-like conditions this week\n\n-  Chance for showers/thunderstorms in Lemhi County and southwest \n   Montana on Tuesday\n\n-  Cold front Friday to bring a change: showers and thunderstorms,\n   gusty winds, then cooler, fall-like conditions this weekend.\n\n-  Frosty mornings to follow this weekend into early next week.\n\n\nIt will be a gorgeous week as temperatures rise into the 70s and\n80s across the region, which will generally be 10 to 15 degrees\nabove average for late September. \n\nA low pressure system will move from northern Nevada to over \nsoutheast Idaho on Tuesday and could help to initiate showers and \na few weak thunderstorms from Lemhi County to Butte. Wind gusts to\n30 mph and lightning are the main threats.\n\nOn Friday, a cold front will disrupt our recent warm and dry \nweather. Despite timing differences with the front passage, there \nis a chance for showers and possibly thunderstorms if we're able \nto warm up enough. If we were to get a squall line forming with \nthe front with embedded thunder, then strong gusty winds could be \npossible impacting recreation on area lakes. \n\nOn Saturday it could remain quite breezy across the region, but it\nwill be much cooler with highs in the 60s. Some locations across\nnorthwest Montana may remain showery with some cloud cover. These\nareas could experience temperatures in the 50s until any sun\nbreaks out. Both Saturday and Sunday temperatures will be near to\nbelow seasonal levels. With the colder night-time temperatures,\nfrost will again be in the cards.",
